# Refactoring guide

## Goal

Break pages into reusable components and unify styling from `app.css` and `src/lib/styles/`. See `todo.md` for the full backlog.

Current priorities:

1. **Typography** — few consistent text styles across the site; finish WIP typography components (`Heading`, `Link`)
2. **Layout** — standardize content width via `PageContent` and `.text-width`
3. **Sections** — extract repeated page patterns into `src/lib/components/sections/`
4. **Page migration** — one page at a time, starting with simpler routes
5. **Experiment page** - Use `experiment/+page.svelte` to show the developer how components will look in different situations using various demos.

## Workflow for each task

1. Pick **one page or one pattern** (not the whole site)
2. Identify existing components/classes that already match the target look
3. Refactor the **canonical page** (Swedish slug, e.g. `paketering/+page.svelte`) — locale wrappers stay untouched
4. Run `npm run check` and `npm run lint`
5. Verify visually in the browser
6. Update `todo.md` when done

## Refactoring rules

- **Preserve behavior** — i18n, SEO meta, hreflang, links, and all copy from `site.js` must stay intact
- **Minimal scope** — do not refactor unrelated pages or rename routes
- **Reuse first** — extend existing components before creating new ones
- **No copy in components** — text stays in `siteContent`; components receive props
- **Unify visuals** — Some visuals are intended to be the same but have diverged. Unify these into one visual, rather than having many suble variants.

## Suggested page order

| Phase | Pages | Notes |
|-------|-------|-------|
| 1 | `kontakt`, `om-mandalon`, `konsulttjanster`, `kunskapsbank` | Canonical SV pages; EN routes are thin wrappers |
| 2 | `+page.svelte` (home) | Complex — hero, carousel, multiple sections |
| 3 | `designguide` | Large (700+ lines), many bespoke styles — do last |

## When extracting a component

Ask: Is this used (or will be used) on 2+ pages?

- **Yes** → `src/lib/components/` in the appropriate subfolder
- **No** → keep in the page with scoped styles for now

New section components go in `sections/`. Name by purpose (`HeroSection`, `FeatureGrid`), not by page.

## Out of scope unless asked

- `analytics_wsgi/` Python backend
- Analytics tracking wiring in `+layout.svelte` (currently commented out)
- TypeScript migration of all route pages
- Route slug or locale structure changes

## Definition of done (per page)

- [ ] Uses shared layout/typography components or global classes consistently
- [ ] No hardcoded user-facing strings (all from `data.content`)
- [ ] Passes `npm run check` and `npm run lint`
- [ ] Both SV and EN URLs render correctly
